~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] How to read the summary
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Each experiment is compared with R2 values reported in the original paper (PAPER_R2). 'NOT
  significantly different'         means the published value lies inside our 95% CI, i.e. we
  reproduce it within sampling uncertainty. p_boot is the         fraction of bootstrap resamples
  that fall on the other side of the reference value (small = real difference).
  The paired delta R2 lines then ask whether adding feature selection (B vs A) or augmentation (C
  vs B / C vs A) truly         improved the model. If the CI of a delta includes 0, the
  improvement cannot be distinguished from noise.
